1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,060
Please insert coins.

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:09,857
The fighting is over, and the big hole in
the protective wall is plugged for now.

3
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:12,157
We finished off the monsters that invaded,

4
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:15,237
and we're working around the
clock to fully repair the wall.

5
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:19,673
Once that's done, the Clearflow Lake
Stratum Village should be safe again.

6
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,781
Thanks for all your work, Hulemy.

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,135
How's the transfer circle stuff going?

8
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,892
I think I pretty much got it figured out.

9
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,480
Even if it's not fully
operational, it's almost there.

10
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,799
We'll be able to send a few people.

11
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:39,360
What a delicious-looking treat.

12
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,920
Would you mind if I had one of those?

13
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:49,760
It's exquisite.

14
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,780
By the way,

15
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:57,337
you wouldn't happen to know where
Director Bear is at the moment, would you?

16
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:02,244
There's still the sunken area near the
wall, and we'll need to deal with it first.

17
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:07,086
Oh, you mean the spot where Boxo turned
building size and dropped in from above?

18
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:11,477
Apparently, the hole I made is interfering
with the reconstruction efforts.

19
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,120
Wait a minute. That shape.

20
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:14,380
I have an idea!

21
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:26,397
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul!

22
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,837
In this new world of wonders,

23
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,837
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner,

24
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:31,750
Lamas.

25
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:33,860
The name's Boxxo. Hello there.

26
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,820
That means yes, by the way.

27
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,500
Thank you.

28
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,980
I'm finally back.

29
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,660
That was exhausting.

30
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:58,880
This morning's rubble
removal duty took forever.

31
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,360
I'm so tired.

32
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:04,120
I'm done over here as well.

33
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,617
There's hardly any air circulation
in the transfer chamber.

34
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:10,357
If I work in that oven much
longer, I'll shrivel up.

35
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,616
I need something nice and refreshing.

36
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,840
Boxo, give me a cold one.

37
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:19,437
Boxo, where are you running off to?

38
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:21,620
Boxo, come back here.

39
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:23,730
Boxo.

40
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:27,577
Hold on, Boxo!

41
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:28,940
Something cold!

42
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,600
Please, Boxo!

43
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:33,240
Boxo, wait!

44
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:42,880
I got you!

45
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,220
That looks like so much fun!

46
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,559
Come on, Hilary, let's get in, too!

47
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:52,240
Hey, hold on! Yahoo!

48
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,622
The water's nice and refreshing.

49
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,640
Oh, good grief.

50
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,357
All right.

51
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,734
Everyone's having fun.

52
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:14,817
Hey, Swori, why aren't you getting in?

53
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,194
The water feels great.

54
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,110
No, thank you.

55
00:04:17,193 --> 00:04:19,607
I'm not really in the
mood to swim right now.

56
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,060
What did you do that for?

57
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:26,938
Making a temporary pool
turned out to be a good idea.

58
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,294
It went over better than ever expected.

59
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:35,657
It was decided we'd hold a summer
festival to give the villagers

60
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:39,093
and hunters a chance to let
loose after all the fighting.

61
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:44,797
Our resources are limited,
so the party is small.

62
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:48,017
But I thought everybody could
use a bit of a distraction.

63
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:51,865
This sort of thing is the reason
why Director Bear is in charge.

64
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:54,420
Boxo, ice cream, please. Me too!

65
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:55,702
Ice cream, huh?

66
00:04:55,960 --> 00:05:00,760
Sorry, but at a summer festival, it's
gotta be this. Let's go! Form change!

67
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:02,460
Shaved ice machine!

68
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,860
Come and get it!

69
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,897
Oh, what is this, Boxo?

70
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:06,977
Some sort of new product?

71
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:07,890
It's click!

72
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:08,997
Objectively speaking,

73
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,597
the quality of the ice the vending
machine outputs isn't great.

74
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:14,277
However, this is where
my skills come into play!

75
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:17,007
I'll shave the ice so
it's like powdery snow!

76
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:20,140
Then I'll add lots of
fresh syrup on top of it.

77
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:25,254
The shaved ice has a distinctive look
that just makes you want to try it.

78
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,648
It's really cold and sweet.

79
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:33,737
The shaved ice is so fluffy and it melts
in your mouth as soon as you eat it.

80
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:34,702
It's delicious.

81
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,760
Yeah, I bet it is.

82
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:41,477
I only wish that I had access to
more than three kinds of syrup.

83
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,390
I know.

84
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:46,615
First, some apple slices from
an apple vending machine.

85
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:50,237
Apples and other fruits can be used
as toppings for the shaved ice.

86
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,150
Voila!

87
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,860
Just like that, it's been leveled up!

88
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,382
Hey, Boxo, what are you selling?

89
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:00,077
Some kind of sweet snack
with fruit and ice.

90
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,640
It looks really tasty.

91
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:08,437
The hunters' association is picking up
the tab for all the food and drink today?

92
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,696
so you can enjoy as much as you want.

93
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:16,120
What kind of magic item
would Boxo be classified as?

94
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,797
It's not like he's a weapon or armor.

95
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:22,460
If I had to say, he'd be an
all-purpose goods-supplying magic item.

96
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:23,940
That's way too long.

97
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:27,220
How about calling him an
all-purpose magic item?

98
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:29,120
Vending machine.

99
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,070
Huh?

100
00:06:31,153 --> 00:06:33,194
You're saying you're a vending machine?

101
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,200
Yeah, yeah.

102
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,397
I was trying to say vending
machine, but that's what came out.

103
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,600
I suppose it'll have to do for now.

104
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,680
Hey, Boxo?

105
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:48,200
Can we talk?

106
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:51,677
Remember that guy you captured
who destroyed my village?

107
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:56,348
Last night, Director Bear told me that
he gave him the punishment he deserved.

108
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:00,120
And now, I don't feel like
I have a purpose anymore.

109
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,037
The only reason she became
a hunter in the first

110
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,877
place was to get stronger
so she could get revenge.

111
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,880
What should I even say here?

112
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:21,600
Look at me, reduced to a
simple vending machine.

113
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:23,671
It's certainly not ideal.

114
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:27,457
But I treasure the time I've spent
with Llamas and everyone else.

115
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,481
I wouldn't trade it for anything.

116
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:30,920
That's why.

117
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:34,157
Yeah, you're right, Voxo.

118
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:37,317
You'll stay by my side until
the very end, won't you?

119
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,640
Yeah, yeah.

120
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:40,740
No more moping.

121
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:44,357
After all, there are still plenty
of things left for us to do.

122
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,270
Hello there.

123
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:51,996
Fortunately, Hulemy and Shimelai got
the transfer circle working again.

124
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,900
You're amazing, Hulemy.

125
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,277
Thanks, but it's not fully functional yet.

126
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:59,797
It's kind of limited to the
dungeon and only goes to one spot.

127
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:02,957
Also, we can only transfer
about three people at most.

128
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:06,497
After much thought, we've decided
where that transfer point should be.

129
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:08,580
within the Origin Stratum.

130
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:12,137
The reason we ended up choosing
the Origin Stratum is because

131
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,997
it's the only one that leads
directly out of the dungeon.

132
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:19,080
It would make evacuating residents
much easier in case of emergency.

133
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:23,857
As for the three people we'll be sending
over, I'd like for you to go, Hulemy.

134
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:24,770
Right.

135
00:08:24,853 --> 00:08:28,797
I'll need to be there in order to link
it back to the Transfer Circle here.

136
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:29,710
Excellent.

137
00:08:29,793 --> 00:08:31,880
I'd like Lamas and Boxo to go as well.

138
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:36,137
Your skills will come in handy,
especially Boxo's ability to make food.

139
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,514
That'll be invaluable.

140
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,340
Sure, sounds good.

141
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:43,057
I've been wanting to check in on the
orphanage and the Menagerie of Fools.

142
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,640
You in, Boxo? Yes.

143
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:49,360
As long as I can help, I'm more
than happy to come along. Thank you.

144
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:52,337
And since Boxo doesn't count
toward the transfer limit,

145
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:54,197
we should be able to fit one more.

146
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,456
I'll accompany them.

147
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:59,700
Oh, it's Mishuel. You're volunteering?

148
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,320
I'll do what I can.

149
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:02,840
How reassuring.

150
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:08,097
I'm still only able to
speak to you, Master Boxo,

151
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,617
and maybe a little bit
to Lamas and Yulani.

152
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,582
What would I do if you all left?

153
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,460
Oh yeah, that makes sense.

154
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:18,400
I apologize for placing
this heavy burden on you.

155
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:19,640
I wish you luck.

156
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:20,980
Please be careful.

157
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:24,380
Alright, off we go!

158
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:40,517
These footprints were made
by humans, not monsters.

159
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:44,659
When the circle wouldn't open, they
must have turned around and left.

160
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,777
Stab anything you can
reach with those spears!

161
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:51,237
Don't line up with those
arrows either, okay?

162
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:54,560
If you start to get tired,
rotate out! On your left!

163
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,717
Roaring strike!

164
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:58,880
Yike! Ah!

165
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:03,580
That's not that bad. Who knows?

166
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:06,097
We might actually get
somewhere with today's attack.

167
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:07,010
Captain!

168
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,550
Reinforcements are here!

169
00:10:08,633 --> 00:10:10,207
I won't say no to some help!

170
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:11,940
God damn!

171
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:16,780
I gotta say, you guys are a sight for
sore eyes! Hey, you lot! Come over!

172
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:17,730
Food's here!

173
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,780
So cold! So good!

174
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,997
It's been days since we had
something decent to eat!

175
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,280
You guys saved us!

176
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,541
Look at them go!

177
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,371
They'll eat through everything in no time!

178
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,297
I'll worry about that later.

179
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:32,674
For now, I'll just focus on
making sure everybody's fed.

180
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:39,280
You're seriously a lifesaver.

181
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,539
We were nearly done for back there.

182
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:45,577
I was about to start pulling out some
worst-case scenario contingencies.

183
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,072
What's he talking about?

184
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:49,382
No, I think I'd rather not know.

185
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:53,260
I can't thank you enough,
Boxo. You're the man.

186
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:55,670
What's up?

187
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:57,690
Huh?

188
00:10:57,773 --> 00:10:59,249
The stairs to the surface?

189
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,430
Hold on!

190
00:11:00,513 --> 00:11:02,186
Are we having a conversation?

191
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,517
So, you finally learned how to talk?

192
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,430
Yeah!

193
00:11:05,513 --> 00:11:07,967
Sorry, I'll have to
update you on Boxo later.

194
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:11,197
Doesn't this stratum have a stairway
that connects to the surface?

195
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,617
Why didn't you leave the
dungeon if things were this bad?

196
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:14,530
We couldn't.

197
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:18,497
The huge door in front of the stairway
was shut tight and wouldn't budge an inch.

198
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,597
Our only choice was to dig our heels in

199
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,237
here and try to hold
out as long as possible.

200
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,150
I see.

201
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:29,590
Boxxo!

202
00:11:29,673 --> 00:11:30,620
Give me vote!

203
00:11:31,940 --> 00:11:33,020
Hang on, Shui!

204
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Hardly anyone in the Origin
Stratum has experience.

205
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:46,084
Even against just those green
fiends, we had a lot of casualties.

206
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:49,997
They might have been in real trouble if
we showed up even a little bit later.

207
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:50,910
Right, Akka?

208
00:11:50,993 --> 00:11:52,337
Yep, that's right, Shiro.

209
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,037
And we were nearly out of provisions,

210
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:57,826
so we might have been in real
trouble if Boxxo hadn't shown up.

211
00:11:58,460 --> 00:11:59,460
That was great.

212
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:00,917
I'll give it another.

213
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,440
Thank you for the food.

214
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:04,017
You should slow down, Shui.

215
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,397
The food's not going anywhere.

216
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:07,127
Yeah, plus it's bad manners.

217
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,380
Sorry about that.

218
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,520
Boxxo, thanks again.

219
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,540
Yeah, Boxxo.

220
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:15,097
We can't thank you enough
for everything you've done.

221
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:16,010
Hello there.

222
00:12:16,093 --> 00:12:18,216
I'm just happy that everybody's okay.

223
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:19,540
I too.

224
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:24,037
They say that when the school director
came back through the transfer circle,

225
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:26,037
she single-handedly
drove off all the nearby

226
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:29,817
monsters all right then once hula me does

227
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,797
her thing and gets the
transfer circle working

228
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:34,377
again we can evacuate
everybody to the clear

229
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,097
flow lake stratum sure
thing leave it to me

230
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:42,057
ah yeah feels good to
finally eat my film this

231
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:45,297
box will hear of a hero
so then what should we

232
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:48,027
do while hula me's
working oh yeah about that

233
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:50,800
Talk about time.

234
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,380
Oh, Director Origin.

235
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,137
It's been quite some time.

236
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:56,100
The magic item known as Boxo.

237
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:58,144
We owe you a debt of gratitude.

238
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,600
Please accept my sincerest thanks.

239
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:04,644
The transfer circle is in your
hands, magic item engineer Hulemy.

240
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:05,700
Oh, sure.

241
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:09,040
Everyone, heed my words.

242
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:12,456
It's unwise for us to stay
in this stratum any longer.

243
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,957
We should prioritize survival and take

244
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:17,805
temporary refuge in the
Clearflow Lake Stratum.

245
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:21,220
To that end, we must protect this village.

246
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:23,977
The transfer circle is
our only path forward.

247
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:26,295
Just be patient a little while longer.

248
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:28,600
We will overcome this together!

249
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,066
I've never noticed it before,

250
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:40,652
but Director Origin seems
especially popular with the men.

251
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,040
The next day,

252
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,857
a search party set out for
a prison located northeast

253
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:49,175
of the village to see if
anyone had taken refuge there.

254
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:51,478
Lamas and I volunteered to go along.

255
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:56,234
